\taxon{Definition}
\title{Reward-model validation law}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{reward-model}
\tag{evaluation}

\p{A \newvocab{reward-model validation law}
#{\mathcal D_{\mathrm{rm}}^{\mathrm{val}}} is a held-out law on comparison
observations used to evaluate the fitted score model rather than to update
#{\phi}. A declared validation statistic may be Bradley--Terry log loss or the
probability that #{r_\phi(x,y^+)>r_\phi(x,y^-)}.}

\p{The validation population and acquisition procedure are part of the
quantity. Accuracy on comparisons drawn from the same collection process does
not establish calibration under a new judge population or agreement with an
independent task-success criterion.}
